{
  "project": {
    "name": {"en": "Kusudama", "es": "Kusudama", "fr": "Kusudama", "pt": "Kusudama"},
    "slug": "kusudama",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "engine": "pliego",
    "description": {"en": "The traditional Japanese flower ball, glued: each petal is a square folded on its diagonal, its corners brought up into a diamond and rolled into a cone; five petals glued side by side make a flower and twelve flowers make the ball, one on each face of a dodecahedron. Watch a petal fold, then press the glued flower and the finished ball.", "es": "La tradicional bola de flores japonesa, pegada: cada pétalo es un cuadrado doblado por la diagonal, con las esquinas subidas en un rombo y enrollado en cono; cinco pétalos pegados lado a lado forman una flor y doce flores forman la bola, una en cada cara de un dodecaedro. Mira cómo se dobla un pétalo y luego presiona la flor pegada y la bola terminada.", "fr": "La boule de fleurs japonaise traditionnelle, collée : chaque pétale est un carré plié sur sa diagonale, ses coins remontés en losange puis roulé en cône ; cinq pétales collés côte à côte forment une fleur et douze fleurs forment la boule, une sur chaque face d'un dodécaèdre. Regardez un pétale se plier, puis pressez la fleur collée et la boule finie.", "pt": "A tradicional bola de flores japonesa, colada: cada pétala é um quadrado dobrado na diagonal, com os cantos levados para cima num losango e enrolado em cone; cinco pétalas coladas lado a lado formam uma flor e doze flores formam a bola, uma em cada face de um dodecaedro. Veja uma pétala dobrar-se e depois pressione a flor colada e a bola pronta."},
    "thumbnail": "/projects/kusudama.svg",
    "difficulty": "intermediate",
    "tags": ["origami", "kusudama", "flower", "glue", "rolled", "celebration", "heritage", "kinematic", "hyperobject", "commons"],
    "attribution": {
      "author": "Innovaciones MADFAM",
      "license": "CERN-OHL-W-2.0",
      "lineage": [
        {"source": "Original MADFAM geometry generated by main.py: the petal's single-vertex fold, the rolled cone segmented into facets, the flower and the dodecahedral ball solved from contact conditions; no designer's modular unit and no published diagram is copied", "license": "original"},
        {"source": "The glued flower kusudama of the Japanese paper-folding tradition: Wikipedia, «Kusudama» — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kusudama (a paper model usually made by sewing identical pyramidal units into a sphere; from kusuri, medicine, and tama, ball; used for incense and potpourri, possibly originally bunches of flowers or herbs; units may be glued together; early Japanese origami often used cutting and pasting; many modern kusudama are modular origami); David Mitchell, The Public Paperfolding History Project, «Kusudama» — https://origamiheaven.com/historyofkusudama.htm (kusudama were originally cloth bags of herbs; at an unknown date the word came to mean hanging balls of flowers folded from paper, often glued or sewn together; said to be one of the roots of modular origami, but historical confirmation is lacking)", "license": "tradition (credited, not copied)"}
      ]
    }
  },
